1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:04,894
SoundBridge，为听障人士设计的环境感知手表。
SoundBridge: an environmental awareness watch for deaf and hard-of-hearing people.

2
00:00:05,124 --> 00:00:09,084
收音、识别，再以画面与振动反馈。
Capture sound, identify it, then respond through visuals and vibration.

3
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:18,286
四路收音，端侧AI识别车铃和鸣笛，同时估算来向。
Four microphones feed on-device AI to recognize bells and horns, alongside direction estimation.

4
00:00:18,516 --> 00:00:22,836
加入手腕姿态，更新相对当前表盘的方向。
Wrist orientation updates direction relative to the current watch face.

5
00:00:23,066 --> 00:00:26,522
触觉唤起注意，视觉补充信息。
Touch gets attention. Visuals add context.

6
00:00:28,550 --> 00:00:33,446
现在，跟随听障使用者小林，走上一段日常道路。
Now follow Xiaolin, a deaf or hard-of-hearing user, on an everyday journey.

7
00:00:34,550 --> 00:00:38,222
骑行者从左后方接近，车铃响起。
A cyclist approaches from behind on the left and rings a bell.

8
00:00:38,452 --> 00:00:42,508
手表识别车铃，用三次短振引起注意。
The watch identifies the bell and gives three short pulses.

9
00:00:44,550 --> 00:00:50,238
小林抬腕，手表更新方位。姿态稳定后，显示方向。
As Xiaolin raises her wrist, direction updates. The angle and pointer appear once the pose settles.

10
00:00:50,468 --> 00:00:53,372
她回头确认，靠边让行。
She looks around and makes space for the cyclist.

11
00:00:54,550 --> 00:00:57,886
比较四路到达时差，估算来向。
Differences in arrival time across four microphones help estimate direction.

12
00:00:58,116 --> 00:01:03,324
骑行者经过时，声源、角度和方位标记同步变化。
As the cyclist passes, the source, angle and pointer move together.

13
00:01:04,550 --> 00:01:09,278
AI还可以区分警笛、车辆运行声和施工声。
AI can also distinguish sirens, vehicle sounds and construction.

14
00:01:09,508 --> 00:01:14,188
背景底噪减少打扰，重要事件以不同节奏提示。
Background sound causes fewer interruptions. Important events receive distinct patterns.

15
00:01:16,550 --> 00:01:22,430
手臂下垂时，先提醒类别；抬腕后，结合姿态更新方向。
With the arm down, show sound class first. On raising the wrist, use its orientation to update direction.

16
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:29,140
不必刻意保持水平。姿态稳定时显示指向，晃动时暂缓显示。
No exact horizontal pose is required. Show direction when stable and withhold it during movement.

17
00:01:29,370 --> 00:01:33,090
角度相对当前表盘，不是身体朝向。
The angle is relative to the current watch face, not the body.

18
00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:39,350
路口车辆靠近，手表识别鸣笛，发出两次长振。
A vehicle approaches. The watch recognizes its horn and gives two long pulses.

19
00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:44,836
这一次，小林暂时没有抬腕。提醒不会就此消失。
This time Xiaolin has not raised her wrist yet. The reminder does not simply disappear.

20
00:01:46,550 --> 00:01:51,086
手臂仍下垂，只表示尚未观察到查看动作。
An arm still down only means no viewing gesture has been observed.

21
00:01:51,316 --> 00:01:57,316
车辆提示持续而未确认，手表间隔重复，并逐步增强振动。
While the vehicle cue persists without acknowledgment, pulses repeat with pauses and gradually increase.

22
00:01:57,546 --> 00:02:03,282
抬腕后显示方向；点按确认，停止升级，继续观察路况。
Raise to view direction. Tap to acknowledge, stop escalation and keep observing the road.

23
00:02:06,550 --> 00:02:12,142
确认提醒不代表道路安全。小林在路缘内观察车辆。
Acknowledging a cue does not mean the road is clear. Xiaolin watches from behind the curb.

24
00:02:12,372 --> 00:02:15,468
等车辆通过，确认路况再走。
She lets the vehicle pass and checks the road before moving.

25
00:02:16,550 --> 00:02:20,870
在安全位置，调整振动强度和文字大小。
In a safe place, adjust vibration strength and text size.

26
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:25,492
重复提醒有间隔和时限，不会无休止振动。
Repeated reminders include pauses and a time limit instead of endless vibration.

27
00:02:26,550 --> 00:02:31,182
另一位骑行者从右后方接近，短振再次提醒她。
Another cyclist approaches from behind on the right. Short pulses alert her again.

28
00:02:31,412 --> 00:02:35,540
小林抬腕查看，转头确认，让出空间。
Xiaolin checks her wrist, looks around and makes space.

29
00:02:36,550 --> 00:02:41,182
SoundBridge，为听障人士出行，提供及时的线索。
SoundBridge brings timely cues to independent journeys for deaf and hard-of-hearing people.
